+FIXED
+
+# cluster ci-78cca41150908714 - builds without FFmpeg could not compile the multi-clip video tests
+
+## Verdict
+
+**REAL** - a test-source portability defect, not product behaviour and not infrastructure. The hosted
+`build / macos-x86_64` job at `cc29a63dde09cf28bb00498a2d2a5b124d4d614d` compiles the video tests in a
+configuration without `ZENE_HAVE_FFMPEG`. `tests/src/core/VideoTestClip.h:50` opens the FFmpeg-only block,
+`:228` defines `videotest::makeClip` inside it, and `:237` closes it, so the helper does not exist in that
+configuration. `tests/src/core/VideoClipsTest.cpp:530` called it unconditionally, which is exactly the CI
+diagnostic:
+
+    VideoClipsTest.cpp:530:33: error: 'makeClip' is not a member of 'videotest'
+    VideoClipsTest.cpp:530:60: error: 'makeClip' is not a member of 'videotest'
+
+The same unguarded helper call existed in the GUI sibling `tests/src/gui/VideoClipsGuiTest.cpp:337`; the CI
+log stopped at the first failing target, so the hosted job would have failed there next. Every other caller
+is already inside the same `#ifdef ZENE_HAVE_FFMPEG` guard:
+
+- `tests/src/core/VideoTrackTest.cpp:298-306` (the sibling `needClip()` the fix follows)
+- `tests/src/core/VideoTrackTestParts1.h:233-236`
+- `tests/src/core/VideoFfmpegTest.cpp:65-69` and `:94-98`
+- `tests/src/gui/ArrangerOverlaysVideoLaneTest.cpp:400-404`
+- `tests/src/core/VideoTestClipTest.cpp:104-110`
+
+## Cause and fix
+
+`needClips()` already returns early when `VideoDecoder::available()` is false, so the helper is never called
+at run time in a no-FFmpeg build; only the compile-time reference was missing. Both `needClips()` functions
+now guard the clip construction with `#ifdef ZENE_HAVE_FFMPEG` and return `false` otherwise, matching
+`VideoTrackTest::needClip()`. The FFmpeg branch is byte-for-byte the previous code, so the multi-clip
+acceptance path (identity/offsets/metadata across save and reopen, legacy one-`<video>` load, `project.new`
+clearing, one undo step per edit, playback frame selection without stale frames, and `video.render_frames`
+across clips and gaps) is unchanged. With no FFmpeg the existing `QSKIP("no FFmpeg in this build, or the test
+clips could not be made")` path is preserved.
+
+Changed:
+
+- `tests/src/core/VideoClipsTest.cpp:524-539`
+- `tests/src/gui/VideoClipsGuiTest.cpp:331-346`
+- `tests/CMakeLists.txt:9317-9333` registers `VideoClipsNoFfmpegCheck` (CTest #977)
+- `tests/VideoClipsNoFfmpegCheck.py` (new regression check)
+
+## Regression test
+
+`tests/VideoClipsNoFfmpegCheck.py` reads the build's `compile_commands.json`, takes the real command line for
+each of `tests/src/core/VideoClipsTest.cpp` and `tests/src/gui/VideoClipsGuiTest.cpp`, and compiles each one
+twice with syntax-only: as configured, then against a shadow `lmmsconfig.h` whose `#define ZENE_HAVE_FFMPEG`
+line is removed. Two fixtures prove the shadow actually takes effect in both directions (the configured header
+still defines the macro; the shadow removes it). The unit is generated with the configured Qt moc. Missing
+`compile_commands.json`, entry or moc exits 2 instead of passing. No timing, sleep or race is involved: the
+only inputs are the recorded compile line and the shadowed configuration header.
+
+## Test matrix
+
+| Path | What is exercised | Result |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| normal build (FFmpeg present) | both TUs compile unchanged; `VideoClipsTest` and `VideoClipsGuiTest` run their multi-clip contract | PASS, family 9/9 |
+| reconfiguration at the cause (no FFmpeg) | shadowed `lmmsconfig.h`, both TUs compiled with the helper absent | PASS (RED before the fix) |
+| invalid setup | missing `compile_commands.json`, entry or moc | exit 2, never a silent pass |
+| boundary | the existing multi-clip fixture covers two clips, a gap, save/reopen, undo and frame selection; the guard changes none of it | covered by `VideoClipsTest` |
+| audio thread | no product or render code changed; the guard is compile-time only | no new work on any audio path |
+| supported platforms | the check uses the recorded compiler (`-fsyntax-only`/`-I` for gcc/clang, `/Zs`/`/I` for cl/clang-cl) and the configured Qt moc | runs on Linux, macOS and Windows hosted shapes |
+
+## Evidence table
+
+| Step | Exact command | Exit |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| reproduce on unfixed tree (RED) | `python3 tests/VideoClipsNoFfmpegCheck.py --source-root "$PWD" --build-dir "$PWD/build" --moc /usr/lib/qt6/moc` | 1 |
+| regression RED, fix reversed (both files) | `git apply -R .../logs/fix.patch; python3 tests/VideoClipsNoFfmpegCheck.py ...` | 1 |
+| rebuild reverted | `cmake --build build --target VideoClipsTest VideoClipsGuiTest` | 0 |
+| regression GREEN, fix restored | `git apply .../logs/fix.patch; python3 tests/VideoClipsNoFfmpegCheck.py ...` | 0 |
+| rebuild restored | `cmake --build build --target VideoClipsTest VideoClipsGuiTest` | 0 |
+| ordinary path | `cd build/tests && ctest -R '^VideoClipsTest$' --output-on-failure` (1/1) | 0 |
+| affected family | `cd build/tests && QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen ctest -R 'Video' --output-on-failure` (9/9) | 0 |
+| registered check | `cd build/tests && ctest -R '^VideoClipsNoFfmpegCheck$' --output-on-failure` (1/1) | 0 |
+| setup failure path | same check with `--build-dir /nonexistent` | 2 |
+| moc failure path | same check with `--moc /nonexistent/moc` | 2 |
+| gates | `python3 ~/.local/share/zene-bunny-fix/qwen/feature_check.py "$PWD"` (all PASS) | 0 |
+
+The RED run's diagnostics name both unguarded lines after the fix is reversed:
+
+    tests/src/core/VideoClipsTest.cpp:530:33: error: 'makeClip' is not a member of 'videotest'
+    tests/src/gui/VideoClipsGuiTest.cpp:337:33: error: 'makeClip' is not a member of 'videotest'
+
+Logs (numbered, in the run log folder): `01` first RED attempt (wrong Qt5 moc, setup), `02` reproduced RED
+on the exact pinned commit, `03`/`04` fixed target build and test, `06` registered CTest green, `07`/`08`
+first reverse/restore proof, `09`/`10`/`11` family setup and green, `12` gates, `14` extended two-TU check,
+`15` both-target build, `16`/`17` earlier reverse/restore proof, `18` earlier family green, `19` setup paths,
+`20` gates after the first commit, `23` refactored check green, `25` final reverse/restore proof after the
+complexity refactor, `26` final gates, `27` final family green.
+`fix.patch` in the log folder is the exact code patch reversed and re-applied for `25`.
+
+## Self-check
+
+- **Regression fails with the product change reverted, passes restored.** Reverted both guarded functions
+  and ran the current check: `EXIT=1`, with `'makeClip' is not a member of 'videotest'` at both lines.
+  Restored and reran: `EXIT=0`. Logs `25a-red-reverted.log`, `25c-green-restored.log`; `fix.patch` holds the
+  reverted diff. The earlier pre-refactor run has the same result in `16b`/`17b`.
+- **Deterministic.** No wall-clock timing, sleeps, retries or races. The test uses the exact
+  `compile_commands.json` entry and a shadow `lmmsconfig.h` produced by deleting one `#define`; fixtures
+  assert the macro is present in the configured header and absent in the shadow before the TUs are compiled.
+- **Fix at the cause and complete.** Every `videotest::makeClip` occurrence in the tree was checked. Only
+  `VideoClipsTest.cpp:530` and `VideoClipsGuiTest.cpp:337` were unguarded; both now use the same
+  `#ifdef ZENE_HAVE_FFMPEG` shape as `VideoTrackTest.cpp:298-306`, and the other four call sites were already
+  guarded. The regression check compiles both affected TUs, so either can no longer regress silently.
+- **No collateral damage.** The FFmpeg branch is unchanged, so old projects and saved data load exactly as
+  before; no format, limit, check or command changed. The no-FFmpeg branch returns `false` only after
+  `VideoDecoder::available()` already returned false, preserving the previous skip behaviour. The 9-test
+  video family (including `VideoClipsTest`, `VideoClipsGuiTest`, `VideoTrackTest`, `VideoFfmpegTest`,
+  `VideoTestClipTest`, `VideoAudioNameTest`, `ArrangerOverlaysVideoLaneTest`, `ControlVideoClipsMcp`) passes.
+- **Gates.** `feature_check.py` exits 0 on every row (log `26`). The check's entry point was split into
+  `load_entries`, `collect_sources`, `prepare_all` and `shadow_compiles`, so no new function is over the
+  complexity target and the gate reports no new item in the changed files.
+- **Realtime/undo.** No production, audio-thread or command code changed; no allocation, lock, wait or I/O
+  was added to a render path, and the tests' existing one-undo-step assertions are untouched.
+- **ALREADY-FIXED / FALSE-POSITIVE counter-evidence.** Not applicable: the verdict is FIXED, and the RED run
+  at `cc29a63dde09cf28bb00498a2d2a5b124d4d614d` reproduced the CI diagnostic from the actual source.
